  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Boric acid <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is a lewis acid,when it is dissolved in water, it accepts <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> from water rather than donating <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> to the water. So,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> it is false.<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> It has a planar structure.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/yeeukayijtxbyqipmhqvhfofvqgzbenhqdydxkiuuwzszwfycc.jpeg\" /><br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> It acts as a monobasic acid: <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">OH</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">OH</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> It is soluble in hot water.",
